      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "As an expert witness, I would advise against consciously altering one's speech to fit a specific standard, as this can artificially reduce the natural credibility and authenticity that a jury instinctively trusts. Research consistently shows that witnesses with dialects outside the majority norm, such as AAVE, frequently face higher risks of bias and are often unfairly judged as less credible or more deceptive by judges and juries. This subtle yet powerful prejudice often stems from subconscious stereotypes linking non-standard speech with dishonesty rather than the factual reliability of the testimony.",
